v4 — Signal expansion + product hardening
  • Earnings estimate revision momentum: analyst target cache tracks changes over time;
    +8 for revision up + coverage growth, +5 revision up only, -6 revision down
  • Gamma Exposure (GEX): Black-Scholes gamma computed across first expiry chain;
    positive GEX = price gravity (informational), negative GEX = trend amplification (-3)
  • Google Trends (pytrends): retail search surge +100% → +6 score; collapse -50% → -3;
    6-hour cache per ticker, ThreadPoolExecutor to avoid thread-safety issues
  • Quiverquant congressional trades: 90-day window, net ≥3 buys → +8, net ≤-3 → -8;
    24-hour cache, free tier (no API key)
  • Sector rotation model: 4-stage cycle (early/mid/late/recession) from VIX + yield
    curve + HYG + S&P trend; favoured ETFs get +6, avoid ETFs get -5
  • Sector rotation bias block wired into signal_engine per ticker
  • Accuracy tracking: /api/accuracy/sources (win rate per signal source) and
    /api/accuracy/tickers (win rate per ticker) — auth required
  • Stripe 7-day trial: trial_period_days=7 on all checkout sessions
  • Stripe promo codes: allow_promotion_codes=True on checkout
  • Rate limiting: slowapi 10/minute on /api/auth/login and /api/auth/register
  • Webhook idempotency: _processed_events set prevents double-processing Stripe events
  • Password reset flow: /api/auth/forgot-password → email link → /api/auth/reset-password;
    1-hour token expiry, enumeration-safe (always 200)
  • ETF scanner expansion: QQQ, SPY, IWM, GLD, XLK, XLF, XLE added to default watchlist
